KZ2 patch 6073: the per-present QPC capture covers a whole run, not only its first 2,293 frames.
Symptom: scratch/present_qpc_<pid>.csv of a gameplay run held presents 1..2293 only (about 25 s:
boot and menu), so tools/runtime/perf/frame_times.py could not measure any gameplay window. Cause: upstream's
ld_present_measure_record dumps the ring once at guest frame 2293 (the end of another game's fixed benchmark) and sets
g_ld_present_dumped, so the later dumps (rsx_live_draw_dump_present_samples, shutdown) are no-ops; and a run ended by
a kill (every Proton test run) never reaches shutdown. Fix: the fixed endpoint is removed. RSX_PRESENT_QPC_STREAM=1
opens the CSV at renderer init and appends each batch of 64 samples as it fills (one buffered write and fflush on the
present thread, after that present's QPC read), and the shutdown dump writes the rest; a kill loses at most the last
63 presents. The stream file adds a second comment line, '# clock qpc=<ticks> filetime=<100 ns since 1601 UTC>',
that ties the QPC to the wall clock, so a window can be cut at an outside timestamp (the run driver's settle file).
Without the variable the ring (16,384 samples) is dumped once at shutdown as before. Same CSV columns. General
(upstream candidate: the 2293 endpoint is a leftover of the benchmark the measurement was written for).

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c b/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
--- a/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c
@@ -905,11 +905,18 @@
 static LONGLONG g_ld_qpc_frequency = 0;
 static int g_ld_present_dumped = 0;
 static int g_ld_schedule_diag = 0;
+/* KZ2 patch 6073: RSX_PRESENT_QPC_STREAM=1 writes every sample to the CSV as the run goes (batches of
+ * LD_PRESENT_STREAM_BATCH, flushed to the file), so a run ended by a kill keeps all but its last batch. */
+#define LD_PRESENT_STREAM_BATCH 64u
+static FILE* g_ld_present_stream = NULL;
+static u64 g_ld_present_written = 0;
+static SRWLOCK g_ld_present_stream_lock = SRWLOCK_INIT;
 #if defined(YZ_PPU_SAMPLE)
 static HANDLE g_ld_present_thread_handle = NULL;
 #endif
 
 static void ld_present_measure_dump(void);
+static void ld_present_stream_open(void);
 #if defined(YZ_PERF_PROFILE)
 extern void spu_perf_window_begin(u32 guest_frame);
 extern void spu_perf_window_dump(u32 guest_frame);
@@ -932,6 +939,101 @@
         g_ld_qpc_frequency = frequency.QuadPart;
     else
         g_ld_qpc_frequency = 0;
+    {   /* KZ2 patch 6073 */
